# Input graph for RDFLib__prez__prez_services_query_generation_shacl.py__PropertyShape__parse_property_path
# written against the region, not against the translation.
#
# Each ex:caseN ex:path ... anchors one SHACL path node reachable by a
# stable IRI (driver.py looks it up fresh per side, since blank node
# identifiers are not stable across two separate parses of this file).
#
# The construction this stratum exists to exercise is
# `if self.graph.value(pp, RDF.first):` -- "is this blank node the head of
# an RDF list" -- translated as `if bool(m{ {pp} rdf:first ?x }):`.  case1
# and case7 give it a TRUE reading (their pp is a list head, built by
# Turtle's `( ... )` collection syntax); case3 and case4 give it a FALSE /
# zero-solution reading (a blank node with exactly one predicate-object
# pair, and no rdf:first at all -- the neighbourhood that must not match).
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix shext: <http://example.com/shacl-extension#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# case1: sequence path as an RDF list -- TRUE branch, and a plain URIRef
# leaf at each position via the recursive isinstance(pp, URIRef) case.
ex:case1 ex:path ( ex:p1 ex:p2 ) .

# case2: a bare predicate path -- pp is a URIRef, the graph-reading branch
# is never reached at all.
ex:case2 ex:path ex:directProp .

# case3: sh:inversePath -- a single predicate-object blank node, not a list
# head: FALSE / zero-solution branch of the same existence check.
ex:case3 ex:path [ sh:inversePath ex:parent ] .

# case4: sh:zeroOrMorePath, same shape as case3 -- another FALSE instance,
# and the neighbourhood for case1/case7's list-head blank nodes: it has
# predicates too, but never rdf:first.
ex:case4 ex:path [ sh:zeroOrMorePath ex:child ] .

# case5: sh:alternativePath over an RDF list -- exercises Collection() and
# the recursive parse of each alternative.
ex:case5 ex:path [ sh:alternativePath ( ex:a ex:b ) ] .

# case6: sh:union -- returns None; its members are routed through
# _add_path_to_shape instead of the return value.
ex:case6 ex:path [ sh:union ( ex:u1 ex:u2 ) ] .

# case7: a sequence whose second element is itself an inverse path --
# recursion inside the while loop, with a non-leaf (blank node) list member.
ex:case7 ex:path ( ex:p3 [ sh:inversePath ex:p4 ] ) .

# ---- repair 2026-10-27 -------------------------------------------------
# The cases below were added by the repair pass.  Cases 8 to 11 reach the
# PRED_TO_PATH_CLASS entries and nested shapes the first seven did not; the
# `err*` cases are the ones on which the region RAISES (driver.py compares
# the exceptions of the two versions, which the harness does not).

# case8..case10: the remaining single-predicate path classes.
ex:case8  ex:path [ sh:oneOrMorePath ex:q ] .
ex:case9  ex:path [ sh:zeroOrOnePath ex:r ] .
ex:case10 ex:path [ shext:bNodeDepth 3 ] .

# case11: recursion through three levels (inverse of a sequence of an
# alternative), and an empty alternative list (Collection over rdf:nil).
ex:case11 ex:path [ sh:inversePath ( ex:a [ sh:alternativePath ( ex:b ex:c ) ] ) ] .
ex:case12 ex:path [ sh:alternativePath () ] .
ex:case13 ex:path [ sh:union () ] .

# err1: a blank node with no predicate-object at all.
ex:err1 ex:path [] .
# err2: two predicate-objects on the path node.
ex:err2 ex:path [ sh:inversePath ex:a ; sh:zeroOrMorePath ex:b ] .
# err3: one predicate-object, but not a SHACL path construct.
ex:err3 ex:path [ ex:notAPathConstruct ex:a ] .
# err4: pp is a literal, neither URIRef nor BNode.
ex:err4 ex:path "not a node" .
# err5: a list whose second element is a falsy literal (the loop reads
# `first = value(current, rdf:first)`, finds "", and raises "Malformed ...").
ex:err5 ex:path ( ex:a "" ) .
# err6: a list head whose rdf:rest is missing ("missing rdf:rest").
ex:err6 ex:path [ rdf:first ex:a ] .
# err7, err8: the guard `value(pp, rdf:first)` is FALSY (the head element is
# the empty string / the number 0): the node is NOT taken for a list, falls
# through to predicate_objects (rdf:first + rdf:rest = two) and raises
# "multiple predicate-objects".  `bool(m{ })` (existence) would enter the
# list branch instead and raise "Malformed RDF list structure".
ex:err7 ex:path ( "" ex:x ) .
ex:err8 ex:path ( 0 ex:x ) .
# err9: a path class applied to an erroneous operand: the error comes from
# the recursive call.
ex:err9 ex:path [ sh:oneOrMorePath [] ] .
